  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Dazzler had an array of NNN **distinct** non-negative integers. Somehow he lost the array, but he knows the bitwise XOR of all the elements in the array. You have to help him to retrieve the array.\n\nYou are given two positive integers NNN and XXX. Construct an array AAA of NNN elements with the following conditions:\n\n\nFor each iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N), 0≤Ai≤5⋅1050 \\le A_i \\le 5\\cdot 10^50≤Ai​≤5⋅105.\nAll the elements in the array AAA should be **pairwise distinct**, i.e, Ai≠AjA_i \\neq A_jAi​=Aj​ if i≠ji \\neq ji=j\nThe bitwise XOR of all the NNN elements in the array should be equal to XXX, i.e, A1⊕A2⊕…⊕AN=XA_1 \\oplus A_2 \\oplus \\ldots \\oplus A_N = XA1​⊕A2​⊕…⊕AN​=X, where ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation.\nIf there are multiple possible solutions, you may print **any** of them.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test\ncases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and XXX — the size of the array and the bitwise XOR of the entire array.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the NNN **distinct** non-negative integers satisfying the constraints above.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2⋅1051 \\le T \\le 2\\cdot 10^51≤T≤2⋅105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\le N \\le 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤X≤5⋅1051 \\le X \\le 5\\cdot 10^51≤X≤5⋅105",
      "0≤Ai≤5⋅1050 \\le A_i \\le 5\\cdot 10^50≤Ai​≤5⋅105",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 3⋅1053\\cdot 10^53⋅105",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (30 points):** 1≤X≤1051 \\le X \\le 10^51≤X≤105",
      "**Subtask 2 (70 points):** 1≤X≤5⋅1051 \\le X \\le 5\\cdot 10^51≤X≤5⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
